The Rust Scene renderer studies linux-wallpaperengine (Almamu), revision
b016d7d1fdcf4e5fd2f9c9fa420a8aaa07fee02d, for format and rendering semantics.
Its former C++ Scene implementation and dedicated source archives have been
removed. The reference GPL version 3 license is retained in LICENSE-Scene-reference.
Rust dependencies and their licenses are recorded in Cargo manifests/lockfile.
The optional Web helper uses the pinned nlohmann/json source archive in
native/web/vendor; its repository, revision and SHA-256 are recorded in
native/web/dependencies.json. The MIT notice is retained in native/web/JSON-LICENSE
and installed alongside the Web helper license.

The optional Web runtime installer downloads Chromium Embedded Framework (CEF)
only after an explicit installation request in Settings. The pinned Linux x86_64
minimal distribution is 135.0.17+gcbc1c5b+chromium-135.0.7049.52 from the CEF
automated-build distribution at https://cef-builds.spotifycdn.com/.
Its SHA-256 is 24ac1980e62be7b1aea2c337d6bd4bc770dccd8b37e47c6db94b397f13ec4dc6.
The Web helper includes the CEF DLL wrapper built from this SDK; its BSD notice
is retained in native/web/CEF-LICENSE and bundled under data/licenses.
CEF runtime binaries are not included in the base distribution. The downloaded
distribution's LICENSE.txt and CREDITS.html are preserved alongside its
libraries and resources; those upstream licenses and notices remain applicable.
